PAIRS = [
(r"""A patrol is a small body of the town's garrison and levy that stands, each week, on exactly one PLACE: a road stretch of its round, a gate, a site, a looked-at place, or home at rest.""",
r"""A patrol is a small body of the town's garrison and levy that stands, each week, on exactly one PLACE: a road HALF of its round (the half on the town's own land of a road to a neighbour, cut at the digest gate — §2.2), a site, a looked-at place, or home at rest [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-17 · SEAMS-r2-8: "a gate" is not a place kind (`ENGAGEMENT_WHERE_KINDS`); a gate KEYS a road half]."""),
(r"""Its identity is positional — `(settlementId, ordinal)` within that week's count — and nothing about an ordinary patrol is persisted: only what a patrol DOES across weeks (a detachment's errand, a loss, the DM's order) is a row (§2.7).""",
r"""Its identity is positional — `(settlementId, ordinal)` within that week's count — and an ordinary patrol has no record of its own: the week's PLACEMENT is written once per tick as a digest every consumer reads (PR4, §2.7), and what a patrol DOES across weeks (a detachment's errand, a loss, the DM's order) is a row."""),
(r"""WC's people ledger (WC-6, unbuilt) is the slot where a patrol's men become a block when headcounts are conserved.]""",
r"""WC's people ledger (WC-6, unbuilt) is the slot where a patrol's men become a block when headcounts are conserved.] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — RULINGS-ROUND2b STOP-PR-0: ACCEPTED as written.]"""),
(r"""TIER sets the CEILING, the one manpower truth sets the POOL, prosperity (and the treasury when lit) sets the PAY, internal security sets the WILL (§3.1, the owner's eighth word). Inside that envelope the war state and the town's belief of what is out there set how many ride this week: fewer in peace, all of them when an enemy is believed near, none on the back roads once the levy has marched them to the war unless the court keeps them (§3.2).""",
r"""TIER sets the CEILING, the town's PEOPLE (the people ledger's census count against its tier's reference population) set the POOL, prosperity (and the treasury when lit) sets the PAY, internal security sets the WILL (§3.1, the owner's eighth word). Inside that envelope the war state and the town's belief of what is out there set how many ride this week: fewer in peace (as many as the court's posture keeps out), all of them when the town is at war at home or an enemy is believed near, and with the town's army ON CAMPAIGN more than in peace — the army's road out watched first, the back roads left unless the court keeps riders there too (§3.2). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-2 · PR-r2-3: the pool now reads population (RULINGS-ROUND2b), and "more during wartime" holds for the case the owner named, an army in a campaign.]"""),
(r"""**PR3 — ONE MANPOWER TRUTH.** The pool is `buildCapacityLookup`'s `facets.manpower` (`deriveMilitaryCapacity`: "Tier + population — the raw body of fighters"); the riders are part of the town's `offensive` capacity, so men on the roads are men not in the field: while the town's army is afield, the riders the court KEEPS on its roads are subtracted from the field army's `offensive` (`patrolDraw`, an envelope field beside ST's `siteDefense`); at home — in peace, or with the town itself besieged — the riders ARE part of its home defence and nothing is subtracted (the walls do not lose men who are home). When the levy marches, the riders are ABSORBED into it by default and the roads behind go unpatrolled; a court that keeps them keeps its rear safe and its field army smaller — that is the decision (§9.1(e)). No second manpower number exists.""",
r"""**PR3 — ONE HEAD COUNT, ONE STRENGTH, ONE DRAW AT DEPLOY.** The riders are men of the town: the POOL reads the people ledger's census count (`settlement.population` — `peopleLedger.js :: POOLS` 'census'), the one head count; their fighting worth is part of the town's ONE strength truth, the capacity model (`buildCapacityLookup`'s `offensive`), from which the field army is SEEDED once, at deploy (`seedDeploymentState`'s `start`). So men on the roads are men not in the field: the riders the court KEEPS on its roads while its army campaigns are subtracted from the army's seed AT DEPLOY — `patrolDraw`, the chooser's trade-off at the moment the army is raised (§6.6) — and re-read only at a re-deploy; the per-tick `offensive` and `homeDefense` are never touched, and `resolveSiegeVerdict`'s stateful `currentEffectiveStrength` is untouched (riders at home are home: the walls do not lose men who are home). Whatever the town does not keep on its roads goes with the army (ABSORBED), and the roads it stops watching go unpatrolled; a court that keeps more riders keeps its rear safe and marches a smaller army — that is the decision (§9.1(e)). No second head count and no second strength number exist. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-1 (BLOCKING) · PR-r2-2 (BLOCKING), RULINGS-ROUND2b: the compiled draw on the per-tick `offensive` "ONLY while afield" never reached the army (seeded at deploy, "regardless of mode") and always reached the walls (`homeDefense = offensive − armyAway`) — the owner's trade-off inverted; the compiled pool read the 70%-tier manpower facet, so population never bound.]"""),
(r"""**PR4 — BY ADDRESS AND WEEK, NEVER A ROLL.** Whether a patrol walks a stretch in a given week is a keyed hash of `(stretch, settlementId, week)` against the stretch's cadence — the host document's own law ("presence in a week is fixed by a hash of the stretch and the power, so every run agrees"); every other draw (notice, contest, look) is a seeded keyed hash with a named stream. Two runs of one world agree on every patrol in every week.""",
r"""**PR4 — BY ADDRESS AND WEEK, NEVER A ROLL; ONE PLACEMENT A WEEK.** Whether a town's riders walk a road half in a given week is a PERIODIC CLOCK: the half's cadence sets the PERIOD (`weekly` 1 · `every_four_weeks` 4 · `every_thirteen_weeks` 13 · `never`) and a keyed hash of the half and the power — never of the week — sets the PHASE (the host document's own law: "presence in a week is fixed by a hash of the stretch and the power, so every run agrees"; the map's own phase is likewise fixed "never from the week", HR:813), so `every_four_weeks` means exactly one week in four — the map's meaning of the word. The stage writes the coming week's PLACEMENT once (`spatialLedgers.patrols.placement`, §2.7), and EVERY consumer in that week — the banditry roll, the smuggling roll, the counter term, the slow half, the witness, the encounter, the report, the map's window — reads that one placement (a pin: they agree). Every other draw (notice, contest, look) is a seeded keyed hash with a named stream. Two runs of one world agree on every patrol in every week. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — HOST-r2-6 · PR-r2-15: the compiled presence was a fresh per-week draw (a chance averaging one week in four — a second meaning of the map's cadence word), and nothing about a week's placement was stored, so consumers at different points of one tick could re-derive different placements.]"""),
(r"""Patrol coverage changes three numbers the world already keeps and no other: (a) a SUBTRACTION on the ONE presence term of the danger ledger, inside ST's suppressor slot and its shared cap (0.25 with sites), floored at zero, never on the walls term — so a patrol lowers only what dens, menaces and enemy columns ADDED, and "peacetime roads carry no danger to relieve" (the host document) holds by construction; (b) a bounded DEVIATION term on the raider row's counterforce — the patrols' actual coverage against the tier's reference watch — riding ST's one additive post-blend slot and filling MN §5.5's slot (2); (c) the fast and the catching leans of PR6 and PR8.""",
r"""Patrols change ONLY these quantities the world already keeps, each by ONE bounded lean at ONE named seam (§6, §7): (a) a SUBTRACTION on the ONE presence term of the danger ledger, inside the one suppressor slot of MN §3.3's composition (ST's sites and PR's riders, one shared cap), floored at zero, never on the walls term — so a patrol lowers only what dens, menaces and enemy columns ADDED, and "peacetime roads carry no danger to relieve" (the host document) holds by construction; (b) a bounded DEVIATION term on the raider row's counterforce, and a coverage term on the criminal corridor's, riding ST's ONE additive post-blend slot under its ONE clamp — reaching a raiding menace's wear only through the stamped counterforce score (MN §5.5 (2)); (c) the banditry ROLL for goods on a watched hop (PR6); (d) the smuggling success chance at the worst gate (§6.4); (e) the field army's SEED at deploy, by the riders kept (`patrolDraw`, PR3) — never the per-tick `offensive` or `homeDefense`; (f) the commons' ONE grievance home, by ONE registered input (over-patrolling, §7.5); (g) the WITNESS read PS consumes (PR10); (h) PR's own WILL gate, by a magistrate's step (§10.5). The hearings and receipts of §9–§11 decide between parties and change nothing else. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-28: "three numbers … and no other" was false against §6–§7; the full list is stated and §7.2's second grievance input is struck · PR-r2-7: MN's slot (2) is filled through the stamp, never added · SEAMS-r2-7: the composition is MN §3.3's one sentence, cited and not restated.]"""),
(r"""**PR6 — THE FAST HALF LOWERS THE ROLL, NEVER THE LEVEL.** On the week a patrol (or detachment) actually stands on a stretch, the INCIDENT ROLL for goods crossing it is lowered by a bounded multiplier at the one banditry roll (`banditryLoss`'s optional `watch01`); the embattlement level — the region's state — is never written by a patrol's presence (item 17: two mechanisms, one truth each, never doubled). Named travellers' rolls live in the frozen roads kernel and feel patrols only through the slow half (⛔ STOP-PR-1).""",
r"""**PR6 — THE FAST HALF LOWERS THE ROLL, PER HOP, NEVER THE LEVEL OR THE LOSS.** On the week a patrol (or detachment) actually stands on a road half, the INCIDENT ROLL for goods crossing THAT HOP is lowered: a per-hop multiplier on the hop's danger BEFORE the route's mean, feeding only `banditryLoss`'s fire test (§6.3); the loss SIZE still reads the unwatched mean, a sea hop reads no watch (no naval damper), and the embattlement level — the region's state — is never written by a patrol's presence (item 17: two mechanisms, one truth each, never doubled; their JOINT effect is one composition with one floor, §6.3). Named travellers' rolls live in the frozen roads kernel and feel patrols only through the slow half — RULED (STOP-PR-1): the slow half alone for missions and sea piracy now; the fast half for missions is a roads leaf-first car recorded as a C7 slot. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-5 (RULINGS-ROUND2b: per hop, never a route-wide MAX) · PR-r2-18 (the joint composition) · RULINGS-ROUND2b STOP-PR-1.]"""),
(r"""What happens next is never PR's second law: a spy goes through ES's one catch; an envoy through the landed `envoy_intercepted · envoy_held` hearings; a hostile paragon through CH's town's-gate words; the party through PT's kind (⛔ STOP-PR-2); goods through `smuggle.js`'s pipeline; a caravan through WY-6's `caravan_seized`; a military unit through PS's witness and ladder.""",
r"""What happens next is never PR's second law: a spy's road catch is ONE roll — PR's notice IS that roll — whose outcome is ES's (`spy_at_target` with WHERE `road`: `caught · uncaught`, the taint cascade); an envoy is STOPPED only as a road hearing, PS's `passage_at_the_border` (escorted · stopped · turned back), never the army interception's `envoy_intercepted`/`envoy_held`; a hostile paragon through CH's town's-gate words at WHERE `road`; the party through PT's `party_gate` widened to WHERE `road` (STOP-PR-2, RULED); goods through `smuggle.js`'s pipeline; a caravan through WY-6's `caravan_seized`; a military unit (an army, a column, a corps) through PS's witness and ladder. Each power whose riders stand on the half meets the traveller separately — one encounter per power (§8.1). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-9 · PR-r2-10 · SEAMS-r2-2 (RULINGS-ROUND2b) · PR-r2-6 · STOP-PR-2 RULED · RULINGS-ROUND2b open question 3.]"""),
(r"""`witnessedCrossing` (PS8) is owned here: a crossing is witnessed when a patrol of the holder walks that stretch that week,""",
r"""`witnessedCrossing` (PS8) is owned here: a crossing is witnessed when a patrol of the HOLDER walks the holder's half of the gate's road that week (the placement, PR4) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-6 · SEAMS-r2-8: per power and per half; a power-blind MAX could not say "the holder's"],"""),
(r"""the crown's riders ride every member's roads only where the crown's hold is `staunch` or `unbroken` (PL §2), and that presence wears as PL's instruments wear.""",
r"""the crown's riders ride a member's roads only where the crown's OWN hold reads `staunch` or `unbroken` (`polityHoldOf(…, rootId, rootId)` — the crown's decision on its own belief) AND the crown's reach into that member is live (`crownReachAt(…).share01 > 0`, which shuts out a sub-vassal under a frayed link) (PL §2), and that presence wears as PL's instruments wear [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-20]."""),
(r"""**PR12 — FIRST TO SEE, FIRST TO DIE.** When war comes, the riders' report is the town's first belief of it; a detachment may screen an invader for ONE bounded week inside the march's termination cap (PS9); then the riders fold into the levy (§9.1).""",
r"""**PR12 — FIRST TO SEE, FIRST TO DIE.** When war comes, the riders' report is the town's first belief of it; a detachment may screen an invader on its town's land — whether the host marches on that town or crosses it toward another — for ONE bounded week, applied once at the screen's verdict and counted into the march's ONE cumulative hold cap (PS9); PR hosts the screen's card and PS keeps the home-defence battle; then the riders the court does not keep fold into the levy (§9.1). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-19 · RULINGS-ROUND2b open questions 1 and 4.]"""),
(r"""**PR14 — THE MAP DRAWS, NEVER INVENTS; THE DOOR OPENS WHEN PR LIGHTS.** While PR is dark the map's patrols are its own picture and its legend is true ("patrols change nothing in the simulation"). When PR lights, the host opens H16's optional door and SENDS its patrol facts per stretch (power · cadence · state) in the window; the map's lens draws THEM, and its legend changes (§13). The host never consumes the map's sway-derived coverage; cadence reaches the map as the host's own fact, never the map's offer read back.""",
r"""**PR14 — THE MAP DRAWS, NEVER INVENTS; H16 STAYS SHUT; THE HOST'S FACTS GO OUT THROUGH THE WINDOW.** While PR is dark the map's patrols are its own picture and its legend is true ("patrols change nothing in the simulation"). When PR lights, the host SENDS its patrol facts — each road half's power, cadence word and THE WEEK'S PRESENCE as it was (the placement, PR4), with state and detachment — out through the WINDOW like every other host fact (the chair's ruling: never "opens H16"); the map draws presence as sent and never recomputes it, and its legend changes (§13). H16 — the map's INBOUND door — stays untouched and open as the owner left it; the host never consumes the map's sway-derived coverage. `patrolEffectsEnabled` lights only where the map's patrol lens is absent or has adopted the host's facts and legend (§12), so two patrol pictures and a false legend never stand together. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — HOST-r2-5 (RULINGS-ROUND2b) · HOST-r2-6 · PR-r2-14.]"""),
(r"""Sea rounds (a harbour's guard boats) are a SLOT on the sea arms (C7: M8's lanes, WY's navalTransit, W11) beside ST's `harbour_works`; the climate band's travel consumer is upstream (CHAIR-NOTES 13). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — R-14.]""",
r"""A harbour's watch is the port's own NAVY (W-NAVY: "One navy per port settlement"; sea battles between navies, blockade as a siege — `navalKernel.js`), never a PR round and never a new slot: PR mints no sea patrol and no sea law; the sea's carriers are M8 (lanes, ports, storm seasons), W-NAVY and seaRoads D-6 (S1–S3). Winter, when the climate band's travel consumer lands (H11's re-version; CHAIR-NOTES 13 as corrected), SLOWS a pass toward `SLOW_NOT_SEVER_MAX` and never closes it — PR inherits exactly that bound (R26). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — R-14.] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-1 · PR-r2-4.]"""),
(r"""the screen rides PS's `TRANSIT_LEAVES` registration list; every lean is a leaf its host calls in ≤ 3 lines;""",
r"""the screen rides PS's `TRANSIT_LEAVES` registration list; the draw rides the one new-deploy site (`warDeployment.js` 685, +1; `warArmyRecord.js :: seedDeploymentState` 72, +1); every lean is a leaf its host calls in ≤ 3 lines;"""),
(r"""`PATROL_ORDER` directs the riders and sets their pay; every clash, join and summons is a hearing the DM may leave, tilt or decide (requirement 24);""",
r"""`PATROL_ORDER` directs the riders and can hold their pay down (the DM's wages band is a CEILING over the purse's band, §3.1 — RULINGS-ROUND2b ST-r2-1's one band law); every clash and join is a hearing the DM may leave, tilt or decide (requirement 24), and the crown's call on a member's riders is PL's `call_in_answer`, heard there;"""),
(r"""The SURFACE shows the deed ("Kell's riders seized a Varn caravan running cloth past the embargo");""",
r"""The SURFACE shows the deed ("Kell's riders confiscated Varn cloth run past the embargo" — the landed branch an embargo gate takes is `confiscation`, PR-r2-23);"""),
(r"""**PR19 — PURPOSE IS THE DM'S; THE PARTY IS NEVER THE TARGET.** Riders keep the roads; they do not seek the party, and a stop of the party is the world's ordinary act on a traveller, its default "nothing has happened to the party yet" (requirement 24's party clause). The world hosts the campaign and never competes with it.""",
r"""**PR19 — PURPOSE IS THE DM'S; THE PARTY IS NEVER THE ENGINE'S TARGET.** Riders keep the roads; they never seek the party of their own accord — they ride for it only when a court's DM-visible `party_warrant` or `party_ambush` (PT's kinds, whose agent is "the WATCH") sends them: with PR lit that WATCH IS a detachment of the court's riders (aim `pursue`, drawn from the round, its cost borne on the round), and the hearing stays PT's. A stop of the party on the road is the world's ordinary act on a traveller — PT's `party_gate` at WHERE `road` — its default "nothing has happened to the party yet" (requirement 24's party clause). The world hosts the campaign and never competes with it. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-13: PT's WATCH and PR's riders were two road forces for one town, incoherent on scrutiny · STOP-PR-2 RULED.]"""),
]
